{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1703 (commit 317ba959c0, Change-Id Ic37749e2bf527f57c02f73b2e59040ba1444be0e, base ae6f2ac57a).\n\nFull local gate set green before push: make lint PASS (ruff check + ruff format --check + complexity baseline + DCO identity + criteria vocabulary + skill frontmatter + zizmor + actionlint), make typecheck PASS (518 files), the standalone check_* gates PASS (adr_numbers, comment_hygiene, config_reads, docs_index, raw_git_writes, readme_quickstart, server_manifest, verify_gate_parity, wall_clock_asserts; check_build_env_locked is CI-only and needs --lock/--freeze args), and the CI pytest lane (-m 'not integration and not external' -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300) exited 0.\n\nNote on the local pytest run: it emitted PluggyTeardownRaisedWarning / 'OSError: cannot send (already closed?)' from three xdist workers at session teardown, but the run still exited 0. That is the same xdist-worker teardown signature this epic's sibling bug fade-ea90 tracks; it is post-results noise here, not a failure of this change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786599087389172001,"uuid":"48b273dd-d182-42e8-9f27-ced5f86acc23"}